\[
 H_4(A)=-2\sum_{\{a,c\}:\operatorname{dist}(a,c)=2}
             S_{ac}(A)^*S_{ac}(A)
 \tag{5}
\]

are smooth finite matrix multipliers, in fact finite trigonometric polynomials before exponentiation. H4 is Hermitian at every angle. The fixed-graph C^k norms are finite for every fixed k. This assertion concerns the full original matter matrix; it does not replace it by its initial matter block. It uses unit rotor shifts: finite-spin ladder weights depend on the electric word, so this is not a finite-spin multiplier identity.

The parent maps preserve the physical Gauss constraint. Equivalently their angle representations are covariant under gauge translations with the corresponding matter charge phases. Hence the bounded exponential of H4, as well as the original birth and loss maps, preserves the physical subspace. The diagonal electric D also preserves Gauss. Working in the full angle representation for estimates does not enlarge the physically evolved state.

Define the exact magnetic multiplier

\[
 U_\theta(A)=e^{-i\theta H_4(A)},\qquad
 \theta=\delta u=\frac{u}{4\tau_*g^2}.
 \tag{6}
\]

For any fixed \(\theta_0<\infty\), differentiation of the finite matrix exponential gives

\[
 \|U_\theta\|=1,\quad
 \|\partial U_\theta\|_\infty\le C|\theta|,\quad
 \|\partial^2U_\theta\|_\infty\le C(|\theta|+\theta^2),
